{"name":"Fancy Pansy","hex":"#bdacca","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fancy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The imagination.","An image or representation of anything formed in the mind."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Decorative, or featuring decorations, especially intricate or diverse ones.","Of a superior grade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fancy"},{"term":"pansy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cultivated flowering plant, derived by hybridization within species Viola tricolor.","A deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wimpy; spineless; feeble.","Of a deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pansy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pansy","blocks":[{"text":"The garden pansy is a type of polychromatic large-flowered hybrid plant cultivated as a garden flower. It is derived by hybridization from several species in the section Melanium of the genus Viola, particularly V. tricolor, a wildflower of Europe and western Asia known as heartsease. It is sometimes known as V. tricolor var. hortensis, but this scientific name is suspect. While V. tricolor var. hortensis Groenland & Rümpler is a synonym of Viola × wittrockiana, V. tricolor var. hortensis DC. refers to a horticultural variety of wild pansy that had been illustrated in Flora Danica in 1777 before the existence of Viola × wittrockiana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pansy","wikidata":"Q12861234"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Pansy_Flower.jpg/500px-Pansy_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th